  "productionCacheFix": "The production request database proxy bound the callable postgres.js $client on each access. This changed its identity and missed the signing-key cache. Preserve the pool as a value, while binding Drizzle methods. A callable-pool regression test proves one key read across repeated requests/signatures. Live query counts must be rechecked after deployment.",
  "frontend": "A covered conversation pool now retains only already-mounted transcripts. It does not mount a saved transcript behind the initial draft or another page. The existing client build has 43 transcript-only static JS dependencies (926740 decoded bytes) outside the App static graph; this is an inventory, not a measured new build or a guaranteed transfer reduction.",
  "limits": [
    "The 3-query intermediate stage kept two sequential waits, so its elapsed time did not improve. The one-query stage removes one wait.",
    "The live first-paint timings in fresh-login-safari-2026-10-30.json predate these local fixes.",
    "No new production browser timing or asset-request count is claimed."
